{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344945-weapon-against-gentry-crowds","id":344945,"title":"Weapon against Gentry = Crowds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-19T10:53:28-08:00","id":344945,"title":"Weapon against Gentry = Crowds?","content":"So I run yesterday day a Christmas-themed session - PCs were running away from their Keeper on mission for him, only to cross their way with other True Fae ( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/314862-krampus-in-ctl\">Krampus</a>, to be precises <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). When the situation in the Christmas Eve in the small town the game took place were bad for PCs changelings, and Krampus were almost there to catch them to his sack - one of players run to the police station and turn on fire alarm. I described that as siren of alarm woke and took from their home curious mortals to the streets, forming crowds - Other left their pray and return from their Wild Hunt to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> So the question of topic: I<b>f in <i>CtL</i> True Fae should be afraid of large human crowds?</b> Would they left pursuit of changelings, if Lost goes, for example, to the busy mall? <b>Side question is if Gentry have a Mask on them if they are on Earth</b> - because I do not remeber this from <b>Autumn Nightmare</b> chapter on them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T11:05:32-08:00","id":344970,"title":"","content":"They can have a Mask if they choose to. But for most mortals, seeing the undiluted mien of a True Fae is terrifying and probably prompts them to run away. I don't think they'd be particularly afraid of crowds - there's no real good reason for it. Especially when, at least according to Autumn Nightmares, mortals tend to forget their visage and true powers and justify what they saw with mundane, but strange, things.<br /> <br /> Though, if by bringing all these extras in the Changelings ruined the story, that may have been enough reason for the Other to retreat. They live on conflict and legends and tales after all, and many of their actions are geared towards exploring, twisting, and retelling the stories that give them meaning. Bringing down a True Fae's show is probably an easier way to get it to retreat than defeating it in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T14:03:29-08:00","id":345139,"title":"","content":"As a rule, unless the Gentry have some particular reason to be upset by the presence of crowds, I don't see why they'd shy away from them. That being said, as a fun aside, I am realizing that the presence of more people means that the Gentry are increasingly likely to encounter a frailty, such as virgin wearing white or a woman with red hair or a priest, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T14:13:48-08:00","id":345144,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though, if by bringing all these extras in the Changelings ruined the story, that may have been enough reason for the Other to retreat. They live on conflict and legends and tales after all, and many of their actions are geared towards exploring, twisting, and retelling the stories that give them meaning. Bringing down a True Fae's show is probably an easier way to get it to retreat than defeating it in combat. </div> </div> </div>Unless he is powerful enough to quickly dispose of those extras because they are derailing his play. Ouch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T14:18:23-08:00","id":345148,"title":"","content":"Or that, but for the sake of argument let's assume they're petty or vain enough to just leave if their careful preparations for an epic confrontation with the Lost are completely messed up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344945-weapon-against-gentry-crowds?p=345139#post345139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a rule, unless the Gentry have some particular reason to be upset by the presence of crowds, I don't see why they'd shy away from them. That being said, as a fun aside, I am realizing that the presence of more people means that the Gentry are increasingly likely to encounter a frailty, such as virgin wearing white or a woman with red hair or a priest, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T02:12:13-08:00","id":348138,"title":"","content":"There are other dangers to crowds. It makes it easier for stories to spread. The Gentry is probably to arrogant to even consider human hunters much of a threat, other Gentry might be curious as to what their fellow Fae was doing. So unless involving the crowd actually fits what the Gentry wants to do (somehow I imagine the PCs suddenly walk into a Dickens reenactment party), I suspect they would at least try to hide.<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could also stick to the believe that the Gentry are actually creations by mankind's dreams. A large group of humans might actually have the strength of will to overcome the Gentry's magic at least temporary. It would be one possible explenation why they create fetches and why Fae are usually only met by small groups of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:05:28-08:00","id":348250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344945-weapon-against-gentry-crowds?p=348138#post348138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are other dangers to crowds. It makes it easier for stories to spread. The Gentry is probably to arrogant to even consider human hunters much of a threat, other Gentry might be curious as to what their fellow Fae was doing. So unless involving the crowd actually fits what the Gentry wants to do (somehow I imagine the PCs suddenly walk into a Dickens reenactment party), I suspect they would at least try to hide.<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could also stick to the believe that the Gentry are actually creations by mankind's dreams. A large group of humans might actually have the strength of will to overcome the Gentry's magic at least temporary. It would be one possible explenation why they create fetches and why Fae are usually only met by small groups of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is perfect explanation I was looking for. From popculutre we see that Fae are a bit reclusive to show in crowds and &quot;not spreadng the rumors&quot; or &quot;the dreams interfering&quot; is the best.<br /> <br /> Also, the Fae fear of crowds leads to changelings making freeholds in towns and cities of humans, where their can hide in populace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-23-2014, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:14:34-08:00","id":348278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternately, you could also stick to the believe that the Gentry are actually creations by mankind's dreams. A large group of humans might actually have the strength of will to overcome the Gentry's magic at least temporary. It would be one possible explenation why they create fetches and why Fae are usually only met by small groups of people. </div> </div> </div>How do you connect them and Morpheans then?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T12:48:29-08:00","id":348475,"title":"","content":"Normally I say an angry mob can defeat most monsters through sheer weight of numbers; but not against God Tier monsters like a True Fae.<br /> <br /> That said I think most True Fae would play along, the torch weilding mob is a classic ending to a monster story, so they'd appear to &quot;die&quot; but profit from their death. You want to actually hurt them, you need to ruin or steal the story. A hero that slays the monster, it's the heroes story. A mob, it's the monster's story. Notice that The Phantom of the Opera's name is the one on the title.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if you guess why I chose that example <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T04:17:47-08:00","id":353599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/344945-weapon-against-gentry-crowds?p=348278#post348278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you connect them and Morpheans then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Morpheans are creatures of actual dreams: the subconscious dreams of mankind. Fae appear to be creatures more of the philosophical dreams: the active fantasies of mankind. The two overlap of course, but it is not as if both Fae and Morpheans are not creatures of contradictions by definition. Besides, whether subconsious are active dreams, when dealing with large groups of people you will get more conflicting fantasies. Of course, you can expand that idea and conclude that if that large group belongs to a relatively similar set of believes it might actually strengthen the Fae. So, the international market around the corner or the large diverse city pose some good protection, but that large group of Civil War reenacters or pagan witches might actually strengthen the Fae and offer the opposite of safety.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}